t_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F3.pic1.16" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#228B22;">Fallback</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 4.89 -310.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:28.07em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="388.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F3.pic1.17" class="ltx_text">Blue: sync, Black: DHT publish/query, Green: content selection</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Cross-server synchronization and content server selection: registries sync records, publish locators to DHT, and client selects best content server with fallbacks.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Hierarchical Skill Taxonomy</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Skills represent active competencies an agent can perform (e.g.,
<span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">nlp.summarization.abstractive</span>,
<span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">vision.classification.multilabel</span>, <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reasoning.chain-of-thought</span>).
In this paper, we represent taxonomy nodes using a dotted notation to indicate the path in the tree (e.g., <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">nlp.summarization.abstractive</span> is a child of <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">nlp.summarization</span>, which is a child of <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">nlp</span>).
The taxonomy is intentionally <em id="S5.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">shallow-to-moderate depth</em> (target depth
<math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 4</annotation></semantics></math>) to balance expressivity and index fan-out. Each skill node has:</p>
<ul id="S5.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A fully qualified identifier (FQID) using dotted path notation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Optional synonyms (not indexed directly; used for query expansion in
clients).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A monotonic semantic version for definition evolution (major
increments ONLY when meaning changes incompatibly).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A parent pointer except for roots.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Skill definitions are published as versioned OASF extension documents
addressable by CIDs. Index nodes reference the CID of the skill definition
rather than embedding mutable semantics inline.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Taxonomy Governance.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Multiple federated authorities MAY publish
subtrees under distinct namespace roots (e.g., <span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">core.nlp</span>,
<span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">enterprise.compliance</span>). Clients treat unknown namespaces as opaque
leaves; this preserves forward compatibility (Goal G1).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Additional Taxonomies (Domain, Feature)</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Besides skills, ADS supports orthogonal classification axes:</p>
<dl id="S5.I2" class="ltx_description" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.4em;">
<dt id="S5.I2.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S5.I2.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Domain</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S5.I2.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Contextual application scope (e.g., <span id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">healthcare</span>,
<span id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">finance.retail</span>, <span id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">legal.contracts</span>). Domains capture
regulatory, linguistic, or data-governance context.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S5.I2.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S5.I2.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Feature</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S5.I2.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Optional binary or categorical traits (e.g.,
<span id="S5.I2.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">streaming-output</span>, <span id="S5.I2.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">low-latency</span>,
<span id="S5.I2.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">hardware.accelerated</span>, <span id="S5.I2.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">eval.safety.v1-pass</span>). These are
intentionally flatter; deep hierarchies would inflate intersection
complexity.</p>
</div></dd>
</dl>
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Each dimension is indexed independently; multi-dimensional queries intersect
posting lists at the CID layer (Section <a href="#S5.SS5" title="5.5 Multi-Dimensional Query Semantics ‣ 5 Discovery and Taxonomy Model ‣ The AGNTCY Agent Directory Service:Architecture and Implementation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Non-Goals.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ADS does <em id="S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> natively index arbitrary free-form
tags. Free-form descriptors can be embedded inside records and surfaced via
external search overlays, preserving core index performance predictability.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Two-Level Mapping: Skills<math id="S5.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math>CIDs and
CIDs<math id="S5.SS3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math>Peers</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Discovery is decomposed for scale and resilience:</p>
<ol id="S5.I3" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S5.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S5.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Capability-level indices map skill/domain/feature keys to <em id="S5.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sets
of agent record CIDs</em>. These sets are immutable snapshots partitioned by
taxonomy node and optionally by time window or version epoch.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S5.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A separate resolution layer maps a record CID to one or more serving
endpoints: (i) OCI registry references (registry host + repository path +
digest); (ii) optional peer addresses for direct transfer (future); (iii)
auxiliary mirrors.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Decoupling prevents high-churn location metadata from invalidating large
capability index structures (Goals G2, G7). Capability indices thus remain
stable even as replication or hosting topology evolves.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Index Object Structure.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An index object is itself an OCI artifact
whose payload lists (compressed, canonical order) the CIDs associated with a
taxonomy key. Optional delta objects encode additions/removals referencing a
base index CID to reduce re-publication overhead.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Referrer Usage.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Referrers attach evaluation summaries or trust
annotations to either (a) individual CIDs, or (b) index objects (e.g.,
quality-weighted ordering heuristics) without mutating originals.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4 </span>DHT-Based Query Resolution</h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Distributed Hash Table (DHT) stores lightweight locator entries:</p>
<ul id="S5.I4" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S5.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Key: Hash(skill FQID) <math id="S5.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> latest index CID(s).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Key: Hash(domain FQID) <math id="S5.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> latest index CID(s).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Key: Hash(feature identifier) <math id="S5.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> latest index CID(s).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Key: CID <math id="S5.I4.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> one or more registry endpoints (host,
repository, digest) plus optional signature bundle reference.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Entries are small (tens to hundreds of bytes) enabling high replication factors
for availability. DHT nodes perform <em id="S5.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">validation</em> by checking that index
artifact digests match announced CIDs and optionally verifying embedded
signatures (preview of Section <a href="#S6" title="6 Security Model ‣ The AGNTCY Agent Directory Service:Architecture and Implementation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Time Sequence: Cross-Server Synchronization and Content Server Selection</h3>

<figure id="S5.F4" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.F4.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="412.61" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 471.66 412.61" width="471.66"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,412.61) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(42.79,0) translate(0,401.86)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -38.18 -3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.8em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="76.36"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Registry A</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 62.97 -3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.75em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="75.64"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Registry B</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 163.67 -3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.76em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="75.82"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Registry C</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 284.5 -4.75)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.25em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="35.73"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DHT</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 382.04 -4.8)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.68em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="42.65"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Client</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#808080;--ltx-fill-color:#808080;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" color="#808080" fill="#808080" stroke="#808080" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -14.17 L 0 -401.57"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#808080;--ltx-fill-color:#808080;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" color="#808080" fill="#808080" stroke="#808080" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 100.79 -14.17 L 100.79 -401.57"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#808080;--ltx-fill-color:#808080;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" color="#808080" fill="#808080" stroke="#808080" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 201.57 -14.17 L 201.57 -401.57"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#808080;--ltx-fill-color:#808080;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" color="#808080" fill="#808080" stroke="#808080" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 302.36 -14.17 L 302.36 -401.57"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#808080;--ltx-fill-color:#808080;--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" color="#808080" fill="#808080" stroke="#808080" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 403.15 -14.17 L 403.15 -401.57"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 4.89 -50.7)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.61em;--ltx-fo-height:0.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:10.22pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="79.4"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Publish/Sync</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -66.14 L 99.68 -66.14"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 100.23 -66.14)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -3.54 4.32 C -2.9 1.73 -1.45 0.5 0 0 C -1.45 -0.5 -2.9 -1.73 -3.54 -4.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 14.8 -58.29)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.14em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="71.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.7" class="ltx_text">Sync record</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 100.79 -85.04 L 200.47 -85.04"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 201.02 -85.04)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -3.54 4.32 C -2.9 1.73 -1.45 0.5 0 0 C -1.45 -0.5 -2.9 -1.73 -3.54 -4.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 115.59 -77.18)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.14em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="71.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.8" class="ltx_text">Sync record</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -103.94 L 200.47 -103.94"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 201.02 -103.94)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -3.54 4.32 C -2.9 1.73 -1.45 0.5 0 0 C -1.45 -0.5 -2.9 -1.73 -3.54 -4.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 34.14 -119.48)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:9.63em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="133.3"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.9" class="ltx_text">Direct sync (optional)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 4.89 -137.09)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.74em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10.22pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="95.33"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Locator Publish</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -151.18 L 301.26 -151.18"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 301.81 -151.18)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -3.54 4.32 C -2.9 1.73 -1.45 0.5 0 0 C -1.45 -0.5 -2.9 -1.73 -3.54 -4.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 105.1 -146.02)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.63em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="91.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.11" class="ltx_text">Publish locator</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 100.79 -170.08 L 301.26 -170.08"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 301.81 -170.08)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -3.54 4.32 C -2.9 1.73 -1.45 0.5 0 0 C -1.45 -0.5 -2.9 -1.73 -3.54 -4.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 155.49 -164.91)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.63em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="91.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.12" class="ltx_text">Publish locator</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 201.57 -188.98 L 301.26 -188.98"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 301.81 -188.98)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -3.54 4.32 C -2.9 1.73 -1.45 0.5 0 0 C -1.45 -0.5 -2.9 -1.73 -3.54 -4.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 205.88 -183.81)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.63em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="91.79"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.13" class="ltx_text">Publish locator</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 4.89 -220.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.51em;--ltx-fo-height:0.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.24em;font-size:10.22pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="120.41"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Client Query/Select</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 403.15 -236.22 L 303.47 -236.22"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(-1.0 0.0 0.0 -1.0 302.92 -236.22)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -3.54 4.32 C -2.9 1.73 -1.45 0.5 0 0 C -1.45 -0.5 -2.9 -1.73 -3.54 -4.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 308.09 -228.36)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.43em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="88.94"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.15" class="ltx_text">Query locators</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 302.36 -255.12 L 402.04 -255.12"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 402.6 -255.12)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -3.54 4.32 C -2.9 1.73 -1.45 0.5 0 0 C -1.45 -0.5 -2.9 -1.73 -3.54 -4.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 299.94 -269.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.63em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="105.62"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.16" class="ltx_text">Return endpoints</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#228B22;--ltx-fill-color:#228B22;--ltx-fg-color:#228B22;" color="#228B22" fill="#228B22" stroke="#228B22"><path style="fill:none" d="M 403.15 -283.46 L 101.89 -283.46"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#228B22;--ltx-fill-color:#228B22;--ltx-fg-color:#228B22;" color="#228B22" fill="#228B22" stroke="#228B22" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(-1.0 0.0 0.0 -1.0 101.34 -283.46)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -3.54 4.32 C -2.9 1.73 -1.45 0.5 0 0 C -1.45 -0.5 -2.9 -1.73 -3.54 -4.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#228B22;--ltx-fill-color:#228B22;" fill="#228B22" stroke="#228B22" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 199.39 -278.3)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.6em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="105.16"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.17" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#228B22;">Select best server</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#228B22;" color="#228B22" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.8pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#228B22;--ltx-fill-color:#228B22;" fill="#228B22" stroke="#228B22"><path style="fill:none" d="M 403.15 -302.36 L 1.11 -302.36"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#228B22;--ltx-fill-color:#228B22;" fill="#228B22" stroke="#228B22" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(-1.0 0.0 0.0 -1.0 0.55 -302.36)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -3.54 4.32 C -2.9 1.73 -1.45 0.5 0 0 C -1.45 -0.5 -2.9 -1.73 -3.54 -4.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#228B22;--ltx-fill-color:#228B22;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" color="#000000" fill="#228B22" stroke="#228B22" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 176.49 -297.2)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.74em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="51.7"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.18" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#228B22;">Fallback</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#228B22;" color="#228B22" stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.8pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#228B22;--ltx-fill-color:#228B22;" fill="#228B22" stroke="#228B22"><path style="fill:none" d="M 403.15 -321.26 L 202.68 -321.26"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#228B22;--ltx-fill-color:#228B22;" fill="#228B22" stroke="#228B22" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(-1.0 0.0 0.0 -1.0 202.13 -321.26)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -3.54 4.32 C -2.9 1.73 -1.45 0.5 0 0 C -1.45 -0.5 -2.9 -1.73 -3.54 -4.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#228B22;--ltx-fill-color:#228B22;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" color="#000000" fill="#228B22" stroke="#228B22" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 277.28 -316.09)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.74em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="51.7"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.19" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#228B22;">Fallback</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 4.89 -390.86)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:26.26em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="363.32"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.F4.pic1.20" class="ltx_text">Solid: main flow, Dashed: optional, Green: content selection</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Time sequence diagram: cross-server synchronization and content server selection.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Update Propagation.</h4>

<div id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Publication flows:</p>
<ol id="S5.I5" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S5.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S5.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Publisher pushes new record (OCI manifest) <em id="S5.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">and</em> any necessary
index delta artifact to its registry.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S5.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Publisher announces (skill hash <math id="S5.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> index CID) to the DHT.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S5.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Peers retrieving the index delta reconstruct full posting list;
negative deltas (removals) are disallowed—removal is modeled as index
supersession with a pruned list.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S5.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CID <math id="S5.I5.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> location entries are published independently,
allowing late replication.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Staleness Handling.</h4>

<div id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Queries tolerate short-lived staleness: if an
index CID resolves but downstream artifact fetch fails (e.g., replication lag),
clients MAY fallback to secondary registry endpoints from the CID locator
mapping.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.5 </span>Multi-Dimensional Query Semantics</h3>

<div id="S5.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let a query specify: one required skill <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, optional domain set <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\{d_{1},...,d_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{d_{1},...,d_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and optional feature set <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\{f_{1},...,f_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\{f_{1},...,f_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Resolution
proceeds:</p>
<ol id="S5.I6" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S5.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S5.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Resolve <math id="S5.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> to index CID <math id="S5.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> via DHT; fetch posting list <math id="S5.I6.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S5.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="S5.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, resolve <math id="S5.I6.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{d_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{d_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>; fetch <math id="S5.I6.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{d_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{d_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Likewise for each <math id="S5.I6.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> yielding <math id="S5.I6.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{f_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{f_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S5.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Compute intersection: <math id="S5.I6.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=P_{s}\cap(\bigcap_{i}P_{d_{i}})\cap(\bigcap_{j}P_{f_{j}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">⋂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">⋂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=P_{s}\cap(\bigcap_{i}P_{d_{i}})\cap(\bigcap_{j}P_{f_{j}})</annotation></semantics></math> using increasing list length ordering to minimize intermediate cardinality.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I6.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S5.I6.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I6.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each CID in <math id="S5.I6.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, resolve serving endpoints; optionally fetch referrers to enrich ranking (e.g., filter by evaluation score threshold).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S5.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is empty, they are neutral. Queries omitting a skill are rejected
(Goal G6) to avoid unbounded scanning across broad domain or feature groupings.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Complexity Considerations.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With sorted posting lists, intersection
is <math id="S5.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sum_{k}|P_{k}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sum_{k}|P_{k}|)</annotation></semantics></math> but practical cost is lowered by ordering lists from
smallest to largest cardinality. Encouraging moderately balanced taxonomy
branches reduces pathological skew. Clients MAY cache high-frequency <math id="S5.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>
lists, bounded by signature or revision epochs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Ranking Extensions.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Base order is unspecified. Optional ranking
strategies (future work) can incorporate: (i) recency of record CID publication,
(ii) presence of verified signatures, (iii) evaluation score aggregates, (iv)
declared performance metadata. These are layered post-filters and do not alter
core set semantics.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS5.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Failure Modes.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Missing <math id="S5.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{d_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{d_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> entries degrade gracefully—lists
are treated as universal (i.e., no further restriction). Corruption (digest
mismatch) triggers client-side rejection and fallback to cached previous index
CID if still within a grace epoch.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS5.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Example.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Query: <span id="S5.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">skill=nlp.summarization.abstractive,
domain=healthcare, features=streaming-output+eval.safety.v1-pass</span>. Intersection
retrieves candidate CIDs whose records declare that skill, are tagged under the
healthcare domain, and possess BOTH streaming-output feature and the safety
evaluation feature. If no intersection exists, clients MAY relax (drop longest
list dimension first) to present near-miss suggestions—outside core protocol but
viable at the UX layer.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.6 </span>Rationale and Alternatives</h3>

<div id="S5.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Alternative designs considered:</p>
<ul id="S5.I7" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S5.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S5.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Single-Level (Skill <math id="S5.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Peers):</em> Collapses mapping but
forces index churn upon replication changes, violating separation of
concerns.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S5.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Full Text Search Core:</em> Flexible but sacrifices determinism,
increases operational complexity (inverted index sharding), and weakens
verifiability of minimal canonical posting lists.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S5.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Deep Ontologies (<math id="S5.I7.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math>6 levels):</em> Higher expressivity but
exacerbates sparse branches and large posting list unions when collapsing
queries across adjacent conceptual layers.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S5.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The adopted two-level model preserves stable cryptographic sets for capability
semantics while allowing elastic, policy-driven replication beneath.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Security Model</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The ADS security model layers immutable content addressing, optional transparent
signing, decentralized index validation, and controlled query semantics to
reduce forgery, spoofing, and tampering risk surfaces while avoiding centralized
trust anchors.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1 </span>Cryptographic Integrity and Hash Addressing</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each agent record, index object, delta, and referrer is serialized
deterministically (Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Storage Architecture ‣ The AGNTCY Agent Directory Service:Architecture and Implementation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) and addressed by a cryptographic
digest (SHA-256). Integrity guarantees:</p>
<ul id="S6.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Collision Resistance:</span> Adversaries cannot feasibly craft two
distinct payloads with the same digest.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tamper Evidence:</span> Any bit-level mutation changes the digest,
invalidating downstream references (index entries, referrers, signatures).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Content-Defined Identity:</span> Identical logical content always
yields the same CID, enabling deduplication and cross-registry reuse.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Digest verification occurs on retrieval before higher-layer processing (ranking,
evaluation filtering). Clients <em id="S6.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">MUST</em> reject mismatched digests.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Canonicalization Enforcement.</h4>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Toolchains SHOULD embed a
canonicalization check (hash-of-hash self attest or manifest annotation)
allowing validators to detect non-canonical encodings that could induce
duplicate semantic objects.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.2 </span>Provenance via Sigstore</h3>

<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Provenance is optional yet recommended for supply chain verifiability. Sigstore
provides:</p>
<ol id="S6.I2" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S6.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Keyless Signing:</em> Short-lived certificates bound to an OIDC
identity (e.g., organization SSO) reduce private key custody risk.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S6.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Transparency Log Inclusion:</em> Signatures (record digest +
metadata) are recorded in an append-only, auditable log; clients can require
inclusion proof.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S6.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Rekor Integration for Referrers:</em> Signature bundles are stored
as referrer artifacts referencing the target CID, avoiding content mutation.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Verification workflow:</p>
<ol id="S6.I3" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S6.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S6.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Retrieve record (digest <math id="S6.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>) and associated signature referrer
(contains certificate chain + Rekor entry digest).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S6.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Validate certificate expiration and issuer chain; check SAN matches
expected publisher pattern (policy-defined).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S6.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Verify signature over <math id="S6.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>; query transparency log for inclusion proof;
optionally enforce Signed Certificate Timestamp (SCT) presence if log
supports real-time gossip.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Policies MAY express: (i) required issuer(s); (ii) minimum transparency
inclusion depth (blocks); (iii) revocation strategies (treat future-dated certs
or time skew anomalies as policy violations).</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Detached vs Embedded Signatures.</h4>

<div id="S6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ADS favors detached referrer
signatures to preserve the immutability of the core record object and allow
multiple independent signers (e.g., publisher, auditor, evaluator) without
combinatorial record rewriting.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3 </span>Trust Boundaries and Isolation</h3>

<div id="S6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ADS distinguishes between:
<br class="ltx_break">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span class="ltx_tbody">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:91.0pt;">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Publisher Trust</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:270.3pt;">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Entity asserting a record’s authenticity;
validated through Sigstore identity or out-of-band trust anchors.</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:91.0pt;">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Registry Trust</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:270.3pt;">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Operational durability and availability provider;
not implicitly trusted for data integrity (digest verification required).</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:91.0pt;">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Discovery Plane Trust</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:270.3pt;">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">DHT peers assumed
<em id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">honest-but-curious</em>; malicious entries detectable via digest mismatch
or signature absence.</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:91.0pt;">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Client Policy Trust</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:270.3pt;">
<span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Local enforcement of acceptable identities,
evaluation thresholds, required signature presence.</span>
</span></span></span>
</span>
</span></p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Separation of Concerns.</h4>

<div id="S6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Compromise of any single boundary (e.g.,
registry) cannot forge a valid signed record without corresponding keys; forging
an unsigned record is detectable via digest mismatch against previously cached
indices.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.4 </span>Threat Mitigation and Attack Surfaces</h3>

<div id="S6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<dl id="S6.I4" class="ltx_description" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.4em;">
<dt id="S6.I4.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S6.I4.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Artifact Tampering</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S6.I4.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I4.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Mitigated by digest addressing + optional signatures; detection via hash verify failure.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S6.I4.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S6.I4.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Signature Forgery</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S6.I4.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I4.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Prevented by short-lived cert issuance + transparency auditing; clients can require log inclusion.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S6.I4.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S6.I4.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Downgrade / Substitution</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S6.I4.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I4.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Old or unrelated records cannot masquerade as targets due to digest mismatch; index supersession uses new CIDs.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S6.I4.ix4" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S6.I4.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sybil Index Poisoning</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S6.I4.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I4.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Large-scale fake index announcements limited by requirement to host corresponding artifact (fetch+verify) and potential stake / rate-limiting in future DHT hardening.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S6.I4.ix5" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S6.I4.ix5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Replay of Stale Indices</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S6.I4.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I4.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Clients MAY enforce epoch or monotonic sequence fields inside index metadata to reject unexpectedly older CIDs.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S6.I4.ix6" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S6.I4.ix6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Targeted DoS Amplification</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S6.I4.ix6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I4.ix6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Capability queries require a skill dimension, bounding worst-case result set size relative to high-cardinality free-form tag floods.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S6.I4.ix7" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S6.I4.ix7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metadata Inference Leakage</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S6.I4.ix7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I4.ix7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Minimal index payloads (CIDs only) reduce leakage; optional encrypted referrer layers could cloak sensitive evaluation metrics (future work).</p>
</div></dd>
</dl>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Defense-in-Depth Summary.</h4>

<div id="S6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
