<div id="S6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">will map threats to layered controls (content addressing, signing, transparency,
intersection semantics, replication diversity).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Performance and Replication</h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Performance characteristics of ADS emerge from: (i) the separation of capability
indices from artifact storage; (ii) the bounded taxonomy depth; (iii) selective
replication and caching policies; and (iv) immutable, deduplicated objects
enabling widespread CDN and registry reuse. This section formalizes the
principal strategies and trade-offs.</p>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.1 </span>On-Demand Retrieval</h3>

<div id="S7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On-demand (lazy) retrieval defers artifact transfer until a query result is
actually materialized by a client. Workflow:</p>
<ol id="S7.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Query executes index intersections; only posting lists and
(optionally) small ranking referrers are fetched.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Client selects a subset (e.g., top <span id="S7.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">k</span>) of candidate CIDs based
on local policy (signature presence, evaluation score, freshness).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Artifact manifests and required layers are pulled from the origin
registry (or nearest mirror discovered via CID locator entries).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Advantages: zero wasted bandwidth for unmaterialized candidates; simplified
cache invalidation (immutable CIDs). Disadvantages: elevated tail latency for
first access to cold artifacts. Tail latency can be partially amortized by
parallel prefetch of manifests (lightweight) while deferring heavy layer blobs
until user intention is confirmed.</p>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Latency Bound.</h4>

<div id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> be query intersection time (typically
dominated by network round trips for DHT index CID resolution) and <math id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> the
first-byte fetch time for a cold artifact. On-demand adds <math id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{q}+T_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{q}+T_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> to
time-to-usable metadata. With regional registry mirrors, <math id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is minimized;
absent mirrors, cross-region RTTs dominate. Caching layers
(Section <a href="#S7.SS2" title="7.2 Proactive Caching ‣ 7 Performance and Replication ‣ The AGNTCY Agent Directory Service:Architecture and Implementation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>) target reducing <math id="S7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> without incurring
full replication costs.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.2 </span>Proactive Caching</h3>

<div id="S7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proactive caching retains frequently requested posting lists (capability index
payloads) and optionally small artifact manifests near query execution points
(e.g., in the Query API or edge function layer). Policies:</p>
<ul id="S7.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S7.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Frequency-Based:</span> Cache posting lists whose access count over
a sliding window exceeds a threshold.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Recency + Cost:</span> Prioritize caching of lists with large
cardinality reduction effect (i.e., (skill, domain, feature) nodes that
sharply constrain intersections).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hybrid Significance Score:</span> <math id="S7.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\alpha f+\beta r+\gamma c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\alpha f+\beta r+\gamma c</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S7.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is normalized frequency, <math id="S7.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is recency weight, <math id="S7.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is
compression ratio improvement (benefit of avoiding another fetch). Tunable
coefficients <math id="S7.I2.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,\beta,\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,\beta,\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> allow environment-specific tuning.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S7.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Cached lists include a weak ETag (hash of concatenated CID sequence); if a DHT
announcement yields the same ETag, revalidation is skipped. Because indices are
immutable, stale eviction is driven by superseding index CIDs—not time-based
expiry—reducing validation chatter.</p>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Impact.</h4>

<div id="S7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Caching primarily reduces <math id="S7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> (query intersection
latency). When <math id="S7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> (skill posting list) constitutes <math id="S7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;60\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;60\%</annotation></semantics></math> of intersection
bytes, caching yields near-linear reduction in total query time for repeated
workloads with stable taxonomy usage patterns.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.3 </span>Strategic Replication</h3>

<div id="S7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Strategic replication involves copying full artifact blobs (not just indices) to
additional registries or edge caches based on policy drivers:</p>
<dl id="S7.I3" class="ltx_description" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.4em;">
<dt id="S7.I3.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S7.I3.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hotset Replication</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S7.I3.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I3.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Top <math id="S7.I3.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> CIDs by query appearance frequency or
post-selection usage. Periodically recomputed (e.g., hourly) to adjust to
shifting workload distributions.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S7.I3.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S7.I3.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Skill-Critical Replication</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S7.I3.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I3.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Mandatory replication for designated
high-criticality skills (e.g., compliance validators, safety screening
agents) to guarantee local availability for governance pipelines.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S7.I3.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S7.I3.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Jurisdictional Anchoring</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S7.I3.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I3.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Replicate artifacts across distinct legal
regions (e.g., EU, US, APAC) to mitigate data residency or regulatory
downtime concerns.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S7.I3.ix4" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S7.I3.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation Cohort Pinning</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S7.I3.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I3.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Replicate all agents sharing a benchmark
cohort to enable low-latency comparative evaluation runs.</p>
</div></dd>
</dl>
<p id="S7.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Replication events publish new CID locator entries (CID <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> endpoints)
in the DHT without modifying capability indices. Clients may rank endpoints
using a latency heuristic (measured RTT, geo proximity) or historical success
rate.</p>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Cost Model.</h4>

<div id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> be average artifact blob size, <math id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> query
frequency for its CID, <math id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> average latency from origin, <math id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> latency from
replica, and <math id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> transfer cost per byte. Replication is beneficial when <math id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(L_{o}-L_{r})&gt;kBC_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(L_{o}-L_{r})&gt;kBC_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> encodes acceptable amortization horizon (e.g.,
target break-even over <math id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> queries). Operators can approximate <math id="S7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> via sampled
Query API logs (excluding PII) aggregated into anonymized frequency sketches.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.4 </span>Bandwidth and Latency Optimizations</h3>

<div id="S7.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Optimization techniques minimize network overhead while preserving
verifiability:</p>
<ul id="S7.I4" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S7.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Delta Indices:</span> Large capability posting lists rarely change
wholesale; publishing additive delta artifacts referencing a base index
reduces transfer size. Clients materialize full lists incrementally.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bloom Prefilters:</span> Optional Bloom filters (or XOR filters)
embedded in index metadata can accelerate early elimination in
multi-dimensional intersections, reducing full list fetches when
intersection is predicted empty. False positive rate is tuned (e.g., 1%) to
bound wasted fetch attempts.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Manifests-First Prefetch:</span> Parallel retrieval of manifests
(small JSON) for candidate CIDs while ranking referrers are fetched
amortizes round trips prior to user selection.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adaptive List Ordering:</span> Intersection begins with the smallest
fetched posting list; if size estimates (cardinality hints) reveal a
different unfetched list is likely smaller, client reorders fetch sequence
to minimize early intermediate set size.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I4.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Compression and Canonical Ordering:</span> Posting lists are
distributed as sorted, delta-encoded CID digests (variable-length integer
offsets) achieving high compression ratios (often &gt;5:1) and enabling
streaming intersection.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I4.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I4.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I4.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I4.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Client-Side TTL for Failures:</span> Negative caching (short TTL)
for unreachable endpoints avoids repeated expensive origin attempts during
transient outages.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">End-to-End Latency Decomposition.</h4>

<div id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A representative cold-path
latency: <math id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=T_{dht}+T_{idx}+T_{int}+T_{rank}+T_{art}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=T_{dht}+T_{idx}+T_{int}+T_{rank}+T_{art}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{dht}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{dht}</annotation></semantics></math>
(parallel key lookups), <math id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{idx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{idx}</annotation></semantics></math> (fetch + decompress posting lists), <math id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{int}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{int}</annotation></semantics></math>
(set intersections), <math id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{rank}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{rank}</annotation></semantics></math> (optional referrer evaluation), <math id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{art}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{art}</annotation></semantics></math>
(artifact manifest fetch). Warm-path removes most of <math id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{idx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{idx}</annotation></semantics></math> and reduces
<math id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{dht}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{dht}</annotation></semantics></math> to conditional validation checks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Resilience Considerations.</h4>

<div id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Because capability indices and blob
replication are decoupled, transient registry unavailability only affects
<math id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{art}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{art}</annotation></semantics></math> for affected CIDs; queries still resolve candidate sets, enabling
fallbacks or deferred materialization.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.5 </span>Trade-offs and Limitations</h3>

<div id="S7.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Aggressive replication inflates storage and egress costs; insufficient
replication increases <math id="S7.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> for long-tail artifacts. Bloom filters add CPU
overhead and memory footprint; disabled in ultra-latency-sensitive minimal
deployments. Delta indices complicate validation logic (must ensure correct
application order); periodic full snapshot indices mitigate drift. Negative
caching risks masking quick recoveries if TTL too long. Parameter tuning (filter
false positive rate, replication hotset size, cache admission thresholds)
remains deployment-specific.</p>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Summary.</h4>

<div id="S7.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ADS performance strategy prioritizes: (i) immutable,
compressible index artifacts for fast capability set operations; (ii) lazy
artifact transfer for bandwidth efficiency; (iii) adaptive, policy-driven
replication to cap tail latency; and (iv) optional probabilistic prefilters and
compression to bound intersection costs under multi-dimensional queries.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8 </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="S8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The reference implementation emphasizes minimality, reuse of commodity
components, and clear separation of pure data structures from operational
orchestration. This section outlines core services, SDK abstractions, signing
workflow specifics, and representative schema extensions.</p>
</div>
<section id="S8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.1 </span>Reference Services and Components</h3>

<div id="S8.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The implementation composes loosely coupled services (each independently
deployable):</p>
<dl id="S8.I1" class="ltx_description" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.4em;">
<dt id="S8.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S8.I1.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Index Publisher</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S8.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Accepts validated agent record submissions, produces
canonical serialization, pushes OCI artifacts (record + referrers), emits
index delta artifacts, and announces DHT updates.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S8.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S8.I1.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DHT Node</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S8.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Implements Kademlia-like routing table maintenance,
key/value storage for capability and CID locator entries, digest validation
hooks, and optional signature presence checks.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S8.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S8.I1.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Registry (External)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S8.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Any OCI-compliant registry (e.g., Harbor, GHCR,
OCI Distribution) storing manifests, layers, and referrers; no ADS-specific
code required.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S8.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S8.I1.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Query API</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S8.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Stateless HTTP/gRPC endpoint providing multi-dimensional
query handling, intersection execution, caching of hot posting lists, and
ranking plugin pipeline.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S8.I1.ix5" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S8.I1.ix5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation Ingestor</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S8.I1.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I1.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consumes evaluation result feeds (benchmark
harnesses, governance scanners), emits referrer artifacts attaching metrics
and quality signals to CIDs.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S8.I1.ix6" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S8.I1.ix6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Signer / Transparency Client</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S8.I1.ix6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.ix6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Wraps Sigstore keyless flow, obtains
ephemeral certs, submits Rekor entries, and publishes detached signature
bundles as referrers.</p>
</div></dd>
</dl>
<p id="S8.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Deployment patterns range from a consolidated single-process developer mode
(embedded DHT + lightweight registry proxy) to a production multi-node cluster
with horizontal scaling on Query API and DHT nodes.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.2 </span>SDK Interfaces (Python / JavaScript)</h3>

<div id="S8.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">SDKs expose symmetrical primitives across languages:</p>
<ul id="S8.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S8.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S8.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">publish(record: AgentRecord, extensions: [...]) -&gt; CID</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S8.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">add_referrer(target: CID, ref: ReferrerObject) -&gt; CID</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S8.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">query(skill: str, domains: [str] = [], features: [str] = [], limit: int = 50) -&gt; [ResolvedAgent]</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S8.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">verify(cid: CID, require_signature: bool = false) -&gt; VerificationReport</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S8.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">get_history(cid: CID) -&gt; [ReferrerDescriptor]</span> (evaluation snapshots, composition graphs)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Representative Python type sketch:</p><pre id="S8.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
class AgentRecord(BaseModel):
ΨΨschema: str          # OASF schema ID
ΨΨversion: str         # semantic version
ΨΨskills: list[str]
ΨΨdomains: list[str]
ΨΨfeatures: list[str]
ΨΨresources: dict      # endpoints, model URIs, MCP server URLs
ΨΨmetadata: dict       # arbitrary extension-friendly map

class ReferrerObject(BaseModel):
ΨΨkind: Literal[’signature’,’evaluation’,’composition’,’annotation’]
ΨΨtarget_cid: str
ΨΨpayload: dict        # structure depends on kind
ΨΨcreated_at: datetime

class VerificationReport(BaseModel):
ΨΨcid: str
ΨΨdigest_match: bool
ΨΨsignatures: list[dict]   # issuer, subject, log_included
ΨΨevaluation_summary: dict # aggregated metrics (optional)
ΨΨpolicy_pass: bool
</pre>
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The JS/TypeScript variant mirrors these contracts for front-end or edge runtime
integration.</p>
</div>
<section id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Caching Hints.</h4>

<div id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">SDK query responses MAY include weak ETags (hash of
concatenated index CIDs) enabling conditional re-validation to avoid fetching
unchanged posting lists.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.3 </span>Signing and Verification Workflow</h3>

<div id="S8.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">End-to-end pipeline for a published record:</p>
<ol id="S8.I3" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S8.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S8.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Developer invokes <span id="S8.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">publish()</span> locally; tooling canonicalizes
and computes digest <math id="S8.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S8.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Digest <math id="S8.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and manifest are pushed to the registry; index delta
artifact references <math id="S8.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is pushed if new skill/domain/feature associations
exist.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S8.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tooling initiates Sigstore keyless signing: obtains ephemeral cert,
signs <math id="S8.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, submits to transparency log, retrieves log entry (UUID +
inclusion proof).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S8.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Detached signature bundle (certificate + signature + log metadata)
serialized as referrer OCI artifact (media type
<span id="S8.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">application/vnd.ads.sigbundle+json</span>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I3.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="S8.I3.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I3.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DHT announcements: (skill hash <math id="S8.I3.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> index CID), (CID
<math id="S8.I3.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> registry endpoints), optionally (CID <math id="S8.I3.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math>
signature-referrer CID).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I3.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">6.</span> 
<div id="S8.I3.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I3.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Client query resolves <math id="S8.I3.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, fetches record, verifies digest, optionally
loads signature bundle and validates certificate + log inclusion.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S8.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Failure at any step (e.g., signature log unavailability) may still allow
unsigned publication; client-side policy dictates acceptance.</p>
</div>
<section id="S8.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Policy Engine.</h4>

<div id="S8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A pluggable evaluation applies predicates: minimum
signers, approved OIDC issuers, evaluation metric thresholds, maximum record
age, required feature flags.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.4 </span>Schema Extensions (MCP, A2A, Prompts)</h3>

<div id="S8.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Extensions define structured payload fragments referenced from the core
<span id="S8.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">metadata</span> map or stored as separate layers:</p>
<dl id="S8.I4" class="ltx_description" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.4em;">
<dt id="S8.I4.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S8.I4.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MCP Server Descriptor</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S8.I4.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I4.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Declares <span id="S8.I4.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">capabilities</span>, <span id="S8.I4.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">tools</span>,
<span id="S8.I4.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">transport</span> endpoint, aligning with MCP registry schema
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S8.I4.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S8.I4.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A2A Endpoint Metadata</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S8.I4.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I4.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Specifies agent-to-agent protocol handshake
versions, supported message codecs, and QoS hints referencing
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S8.I4.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S8.I4.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt Bundle</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S8.I4.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I4.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Versioned collection of prompt templates (system, task,
evaluation) with hashing for each template enabling selective reuse.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S8.I4.ix4" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S8.I4.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation Metrics</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S8.I4.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I4.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Structured vector (e.g., latency p95, factuality
score, safety pass ratio) enabling future machine-readable ranking
strategies.</p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="S8.I4.ix5" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S8.I4.ix5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Composition Graph</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S8.I4.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I4.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DAG describing multi-agent orchestration or tool
chaining (nodes reference constituent agent CIDs) enabling reproducible
compound behaviors.</p>
</div></dd>
</dl>
<p id="S8.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Each extension is assigned a globally unique media type and schema URL. Unknown
extensions are safely ignored by baseline clients, preserving forward
compatibility (Goal G1).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S9" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">9 </span>Related Work</h2>

<div id="S9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Efforts to structure discovery and interoperability across emerging AI agent
ecosystems span naming systems, interoperability protocols, identity primitives,
and artifact distribution substrates. We situate ADS with respect to these
dimensions.</p>
</div>
<section id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Naming and Index Resolution.</h4>

<div id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The NANDA corpus
 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>
 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>
 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>
 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>
 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>
argues for DNS-inspired hierarchical naming, adaptive resolution strategies, and
enterprise governance layers for an “Internet of AI Agents.” ADS is
complementary: it does not attempt to standardize mnemonic names or resolver
behaviors, instead treating any external name or handle as an input that
ultimately resolves (directly or indirectly) to capability-bearing,
content-addressed records (CIDs). Where NANDA focuses on resolver adaptability
and governance surface, ADS emphasizes capability taxonomy intersection and
cryptographic object immutability. A future interoperability path envisions name
resolution (NANDA) yielding a capability query or CID seed refined via ADS’s
multi-dimensional indices.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Interoperability Protocol Registries.</h4>

<div id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Model Context Protocol
registry <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> catalogs MCP servers and tools but
does not define a multi-dimensional capability taxonomy nor a distributed
two-level mapping separating capability indices from storage peers. The A2A
initiative <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite> introduces protocol-level interoperability
for agent communication; ADS instead targets discovery semantics independent of
runtime messaging protocols. Proposed blockchain-oriented approaches (e.g.,
ERC-8004 trustless agents <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>) explore on-chain attestations and
economic primitives; ADS reuses off-chain content distribution for performance
and cost efficiency while enabling cryptographic verification through signatures
and digests.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Content Distribution and Artifact Reuse.</h4>

<div id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">OCI distribution
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite> and ORAS tooling have demonstrated robust
scalability for immutable artifact delivery in container and artifact
ecosystems. ADS directly reuses these semantics (push/pull/referrers, digest
addressing) rather than introducing a bespoke transport, enabling transparent
adoption of registry caching, access policies, and scanning workflows. This
differs from proposals centered purely on hierarchical name delegation that do
not intrinsically bind names to verifiable digests.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Decentralized Routing and Lookup.</h4>

<div id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DHT-based routing (e.g., Kademlia
deployments underpinning IPFS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>) informs ADS’s design for
distributing responsibility of capability-to-CID and CID-to-peer mappings.
Unlike generic content routing, ADS constrains query structure (must include at
least one skill dimension) to preserve bounded intersection complexity (Goal G6)
while allowing federation without global mirroring.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Identity, Integrity, and Provenance.</h4>

<div id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Identity-focused initiatives
(Microsoft Entra Agent ID <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>) address enterprise lifecycle
management, credential binding, and governance. ADS focuses on artifact-level
immutability (CIDs) and optional signing (Sigstore integration, forthcoming
section) rather than operator directory management. These layers can compose:
organizational identity services can publish or sign ADS records; ADS does not
prescribe identity issuance mechanisms.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Schema Frameworks and Extensibility.</h4>

<div id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Open Agentic Schema
Framework (OASF) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite> provides a structured, versioned extension surface
analogous in spirit to security telemetry unification efforts (e.g., OCSF
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>). ADS leverages this to keep the core record minimal while enabling
additive enrichment (evaluations, MCP descriptors, prompt bundles) without
forking the base schema.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Comparative Focus.</h4>

<div id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Summarizing: (i) naming/index proposals (NANDA)
optimize human-friendly and governance-aware resolution; (ii) interoperability
protocols (MCP, A2A) facilitate runtime context and message exchange; (iii)
identity systems manage agent lifecycle credentials; (iv) on-chain proposals
introduce economic/trust anchoring; (v) ADS centers on scalable,
capability-centric, content-addressed discovery with federated, storage-agnostic
indices. These strata are complementary and layered rather than mutually
exclusive.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Comparison: Semantic Description of Agent Capabilities.</h4>

<div id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S9.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Comparison: Semantic Description of Agent Capabilities. ‣ 9 Related Work ‣ The AGNTCY Agent Directory Service:Architecture and Implementation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> compares MCP, A2A, and NANDA with respect to their support for semantic description of AI agent capabilities (skills, taxonomies, extensibility, and related axes):</p>
</div>
<figure id="S9.T2" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S9.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S9.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S9.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">oprule
extbfSystem</th>
<th id="S9.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S9.T2.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Skill/Capability Semantics</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S9.T2.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S9.T2.2.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Taxonomy Support</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S9.T2.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S9.T2.2.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Extensibility</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S9.T2.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S9.T2.2.1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Notes</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S9.T2.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S9.T2.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">MCP</th>
<td id="S9.T2.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Structured (capabilities, tools, endpoints)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S9.T2.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Flat or ad-hoc lists</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S9.T2.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.2.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Moderate (schema extensions)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S9.T2.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.2.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Focus on runtime context, not deep skill taxonomy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S9.T2.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S9.T2.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">A2A</th>
<td id="S9.T2.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Protocol-level (supported messages, codecs)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S9.T2.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Minimal (feature flags)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S9.T2.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.3.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.3.4.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Limited</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S9.T2.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.3.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.3.5.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Emphasizes agent comms, not capability semantics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S9.T2.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S9.T2.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">NANDA</th>
<td id="S9.T2.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Hierarchical (DNS-inspired names, skills)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S9.T2.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Strong (multi-level, governance-aware)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S9.T2.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.4.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.4.4.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">High (adaptive, federated)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S9.T2.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.4.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.4.5.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Focus on naming, resolver adaptability, and governance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S9.T2.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S9.T2.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">ADS</th>
<td id="S9.T2.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Structured (OASF, skills, domains, features)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S9.T2.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Hierarchical, multi-dimensional</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S9.T2.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.5.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">High (schema, referrers, extensions)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S9.T2.2.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="S9.T2.2.5.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S9.T2.2.5.5.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Capability-centric, content-addressed, federated indices</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Comparison of MCP, A2A, NANDA, and ADS on semantic description of agent capabilities.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S10" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">10 </span>Future Work</h2>

<div id="S10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ADS opens several avenues for future research and development:</p>
<ul id="S10.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S10.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S10.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S10.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interoperability with Naming Systems:</span> Integrating ADS with DNS-inspired agent naming and resolution (e.g., NANDA) to enable seamless capability-centric and mnemonic queries.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S10.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S10.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S10.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Advanced Ranking and Evaluation:</span> Developing richer evaluation metrics, ranking strategies, and trust signals for agent selection, including machine-readable benchmarks and governance overlays.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S10.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S10.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S10.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Privacy and Confidentiality Extensions:</span> Supporting encrypted referrer layers and privacy-preserving evaluation sharing for sensitive agent metadata.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S10.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S10.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S10.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Federated Governance:</span> Exploring policy-driven federation, cross-domain trust anchors, and compliance mechanisms for multi-jurisdictional deployments.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S10.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S10.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S10.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Performance Optimization:</span> Implementing adaptive caching, replication, and query acceleration techniques for large-scale, low-latency agent discovery.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S10.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S10.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S10.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Schema Evolution:</span> Formalizing extension registries and versioning strategies for OASF and related schema surfaces to support emerging agent modalities.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S10.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S10.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S10.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S10.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Open Source Tooling:</span> Expanding SDKs, reference implementations, and developer tooling for broader adoption and community-driven innovation.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S11" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">11 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The AGNTCY Agent Directory Service (ADS) provides a scalable, capability-centric, and content-addressed foundation for agent discovery in multi-agent systems. By leveraging the Open Agentic Schema Framework (OASF), OCI registry infrastructure, and cryptographic signing, ADS enables efficient, verifiable, and extensible indexing of agent capabilities, domains, and features. Its layered architecture decouples capability indices from artifact storage, supporting federated operation, adaptive replication, and multi-dimensional queries. ADS complements parallel efforts in agent naming, interoperability, and identity, and is designed for forward compatibility and integration with emerging standards. Ongoing work will further enhance interoperability, ranking, privacy, and performance, positioning ADS as a foundational component for the next generation of agentic ecosystems.</p>
</div>
</section>
